    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d404">

                <pb facs="0333" n="324" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg324"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C115/1430: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-07-14T17:00:00+01:00">July 14, 1940—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 14—11:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2160. Winant informs me very confidentially that he proposes, with support of the
                    Foreign Office here, to move International Labor Office to Canada if the
                    Canadian Government is agreeable and that Massey<anchor n="22" xml:id="d404-f1"
                    /> is today telegraphing Ottawa recommending that an invitation be issued.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d404-f1" n="22" xml:id="d404-f1-content">
                <p>Vincent Massey, Canadian High Commissioner at London.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
